    "text": "Topic 31 -- First Order Linear Equations \nDefinition of Linear \nIn a linear equation, the dependent variable and its derivatives \nare of first degree (i.e. raised to the first power).  Any \ncoefficients depend only on the independent variable. \nExample 1 \nIs it linear? \n \uD835\uDC66\u2032\u2032 \u002B 3\uD835\uDC65\uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B 17\uD835\uDC66 = 0   \uD835\uDC66\u2032\u2032 \u002B 3\uD835\uDC66\uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B 17\uD835\uDC66 = 0",
    "tokenCount": 50,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260728035346-bb3feffd56:chunk-0003",
    "ordinal": 3,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 3",
    "text": "3\uD835\uDC65\uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B sin \uD835\uDC66 = 0    \uD835\uDC66\u2032\u2032 \u002B \uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B\n17\n\uD835\uDC66 = 0",
    "tokenCount": 5,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260728035346-bb3feffd56:chunk-0004",
    "ordinal": 4,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 4",
    "text": "\uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B 17\uD835\uDC66 = \uD835\uDC52\uD835\uDC65     \uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B 17\uD835\uDC66 = \uD835\uDC52\uD835\uDC66",
    "tokenCount": 2,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260728035346-bb3feffd56:chunk-0005",
    "ordinal": 5,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 5",
    "text": "# PAGE 2\nPage 2 of 5",
    "tokenCount": 6,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260728035346-bb3feffd56:chunk-0006",
    "ordinal": 6,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 6",
    "text": "Definition of First-Order Linear \nA first-order linear equation is an equation that may be written in the \nform: \n\uD835\uDC51\uD835\uDC66\n\uD835\uDC51\uD835\uDC65 \u002B \uD835\uDC43(\uD835\uDC65)\uD835\uDC66 = \uD835\uDC44(\uD835\uDC65)  or   \uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B \uD835\uDC43(\uD835\uDC65)\uD835\uDC66 = \uD835\uDC44(\uD835\uDC65)",
    "tokenCount": 19,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260728035346-bb3feffd56:chunk-0007",
    "ordinal": 7,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 7",
    "text": "Example 2 \nSolve: \uD835\uDC66\u2032 \u002B\n3\n\uD835\uDC65 \uD835\uDC66 = \uD835\uDC654",
    "tokenCount": 5,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
